{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CROSS-REFERENCE from the epic 2ddd run: this bug was observed TWICE before it was root-caused, and both observations are the same mechanism.\n\n1. While verifying story 73b8's own AC8 (the criterion 'the default tier stays clean under the budget'), I ran 'pytest -m unit -n 4 --dist worksteal' on merged main and got: 1 failed, 5430 passed, with \"worker 'gw0' crashed while running tests/unit/grounding/test_conformance.py::test_opengrep_timeout_via_harness\" and ZERO occurrences of 'Failed: Timeout'. That test passes in isolation in 44.46s. I recorded the datum on task 7da8-9d47-9604-4257 (lead-unpleasing-kitten), which owns that test, and explicitly declined to assert a cause from one occurrence.\n\nThat observation is now explained: 44.46s against a 20s budget, and thread-method expiry is os._exit(1) rather than a verdict, so the zero 'Failed: Timeout' was a PREDICTION of the mechanism rather than evidence against it. Worth noting the near-miss - the crash was visible in the same session the budget landed, and I ticked AC8 on its literal terms ('reports no Failed: Timeout') while recording the anomaly separately. The criterion was satisfiable precisely BECAUSE the failure mode cannot produce that string. An oracle keyed on 'no Failed: Timeout' is blind to exactly this bug.\n\n2. The epic's remaining change, Gerrit 2098 (story 3436, compact-planner consolidation), was reported as 'CI failed' and investigated as if it were the cause. It is exonerated: both failing CI runs carry headSha 6a5c88027c5, i.e. main itself, and 2098 touches only compact_*.py plus two compact tests.\n\nThe silent-test-drop finding deserves emphasis for whoever reviews the fix: crashing workers dropped outcomes (95 vs 183 locally, 16175 vs 16182 in CI). For the window this was live, the suite was not merely red - it was reporting fewer results than it ran, so a genuine failure in a dropped test would have gone unseen."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787420303089362001,"uuid":"3abe1843-0359-4dcf-8791-8a946b6b56a5"}